# CQ-22  What sequence of device commands implements a curtailment instruction?
# Group F -- SHIFT is EXPECTED TO FAIL this.
#
# Parameters (method note 5): the service whose curtailment is being decomposed.
#
# MISSING TERM. SHIFT has no command model. It declares shift:ControlAsset,
# shift:controlsAsset and the datatype shift:activationSignalType, but:
#   - there is no Command class, so an individual instruction cannot be
#     represented at all -- only a signal TYPE string on the control asset;
#   - there is no Function class binding a command to the device capability
#     it invokes;
#   - there is no ordering or sequencing property (no next/step/position), so
#     even if commands existed, "sequence" could not be expressed.
# The nearest SAREF equivalents are saref:Command, saref:Function and
# saref:actsUpon, with ordering left to the profile. Missing terms:
# saref:Command, saref:Function, plus a step-ordering property.
#
# The query below is the closest SHIFT admits and returns nothing.
PREFIX shift: <https://w3id.org/shift/core#>
PREFIX xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
SELECT ?service ?controlAsset ?activationSignalType
WHERE {
  # -- parameters --------------------------------------------------------
  VALUES ?SERVICE { <https://w3id.org/shift/kg/service/S000> }
  # ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  BIND(?SERVICE AS ?service)
  ?SERVICE a shift:FlexibilityService .
  ?controlAsset a shift:ControlAsset ;
                shift:controlsAsset ?controlledAsset ;
                shift:activationSignalType ?activationSignalType .
  ?controlledAsset shift:usedInFlexService ?SERVICE .
}
ORDER BY ?controlAsset
